<!--
  Public marketing home page ("/", signed-out only -- HomeWebController
  redirects a signed-in visitor to /feed before this ever renders). M7,
  added after the M6 PR merged at the user's request to "get more of the
  base app done" and to "replicate what currently exists" on the live
  expatevents.net site, "mimicking the new design documents for styling".

  Content below (hero copy, value props, pricing copy, groups explainer,
  footer) is reproduced from the live expatevents.net site as read
  directly in-browser on 2026-09-23. Layout/visual styling comes from the
  design canvas's Home artboard (Main.dc.html), documented in
  docs/design-system.md -- see Public/css/home.css's own header comment
  for why that styling lives in a separate stylesheet rather than a
  \#import("body")-style <style> block here.

  Two deliberate deviations from a literal copy of the live site, made
  after the human server-checkpoint:
  - The nav's "Register" button is gone. The live site's Register flow
    doesn't exist here -- sign-in is Apple/Google only until M3 adds
    passkeys, and a "Register" button that just points at /login (the
    same place "Log in" goes) is misleading, not a placeholder worth
    keeping. Tracked as a to-do for M3, which is where a real
    registration entry point belongs.
  - The hero's primary "Get Started" CTA goes to /events, not /login.
    Browsing events is public and doesn't require signing in first, so
    routing the site's main CTA through a login wall was the actual bug
    -- the pricing section's two CTAs ("Get started free" / "Sign in to
    upgrade") still correctly go to /login, since upgrading/signing up
    is what those are for.

  Deliberately does NOT \#extend("layouts/base") -- that layout's nav is
  plain Tailwind utility classes and only makes sense once someone is
  inside the signed-in app shell; this page is the one screen in the
  codebase actually built from the design canvas's own nav/hero/section
  components, and nesting the two would fight visually. Every other page
  keeps extending layouts/base -- see MILESTONES.md's incremental-design-
  system-rollout note.

  Every icon below is inlined as its own <svg><path.../></svg> rather than
  a shared <symbol>+<use href="\#i-name"> sprite (the canvas's own
  approach) -- a <use href="\#..."> puts a bare "\#identifier" in an
  attribute value, which is exactly the LeafKit misparse class already
  hit once in this codebase (partials/event-fragment.leaf, M4:
  hx-target="\#event-fragment"). Inlining sidesteps the whole class of bug
  instead of relying on remembering to escape it.
-->
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>ExpatEvents — Helping expats get together</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/home.css">
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">

  <nav class="nav">
    <div class="nav-inner">
      <a class="brand" href="/"><img src="/design/logo.png" alt=""><span>ExpatEvents</span></a>
      <div class="nav-links">
        <a class="nav-link" href="/events">Events</a>
        <a class="nav-link" href="/groups">Groups</a>
        <a class="nav-link" href="\#pricing">Pricing</a>
      </div>
      <div class="nav-actions">
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/login">Log in</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-inner">
      <div>
        <span class="hero-eyebrow"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="width:14px;height:14px"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.5"/><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="3.6" ry="8.5"/><line x1="3.7" y1="9.5" x2="20.3" y2="9.5"/><line x1="3.7" y1="14.5" x2="20.3" y2="14.5"/></svg> Built for expats, everywhere</span>
        <h1>Welcome to<br/>ExpatEvents</h1>
        <p class="lede">Host and find events in your local area &mdash; or the place you're visiting next. We help expats build a real community in a new country.</p>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a class="btn btn-solid-light" href="/events" style="padding:14px 26px;font-size:15.5px;">Get Started <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="width:16px;height:16px"><line x1="4" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/><polyline points="13 6 19 12 13 18"/></svg></a>
          <span class="hero-scroll">Scroll down to learn more ↓</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-visual">
        <img class="hv-1" src="/design/categories/travel.jpg" alt="">
        <img class="hv-2" src="/design/categories/culture.jpg" alt="">
        <div class="hv-badge">
          <span class="dot"></span>
          <div><b>#(activeEventCount) events on ExpatEvents</b><span>Reflects live event data</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head" style="margin-bottom:0;">
        <span class="eyebrow">Why ExpatEvents</span>
        <h2>A community built for people starting over</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="values">
        <div class="card value-card">
          <div class="value-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="9" cy="8.5" r="3.2"/><path d="M2.8 20c0-3.4 2.8-5.7 6.2-5.7s6.2 2.3 6.2 5.7"/><circle cx="17.2" cy="9.2" r="2.4"/><path d="M21.2 20c0-2.6-1.9-4.6-4.4-5.3"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Helping expats get together</h3>
          <p>We provide a way to host and find events in your local area or a place you're visiting. Our goal is to help expats build and foster community in their new country.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card value-card">
          <div class="value-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3.5" y="5" width="17" height="16" rx="2.5"/><line x1="3.5" y1="9.5" x2="20.5" y2="9.5"/><line x1="8" y1="3" x2="8" y2="7"/><line x1="16" y1="3" x2="16" y2="7"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Host your event with us</h3>
          <p>We're focused on serving the expat community. When you host with us, you reach other expats only &mdash; no competing with generic events not meant for you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card value-card">
          <div class="value-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="10.8" cy="10.8" r="6.3"/><line x1="15.5" y1="15.5" x2="20.5" y2="20.5"/></svg></div>
          <h3>Find an event with other expats</h3>
          <p>Moving abroad is tough &mdash; new language, no support network, an unfamiliar system. Find events near you and make new friends in your new home.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section pricing-wrap" id="pricing">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Pricing</span>
        <h2>Simple plans, no surprises</h2>
        <p>Start free. Upgrade any time to host without limits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pricing-grid">
        <div class="card price-card">
          <div class="price-tier">Free</div>
          <div class="price-amount"><b>$0</b><span>forever</span></div>
          <div class="price-alt">&nbsp;</div>
          <ul class="price-list">
            <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Host up to 5 active events</li>
            <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Up to 5 attendees per hosted event</li>
            <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Public events only</li>
            <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Join any public event, or private events you're invited to</li>
            <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Past &amp; cancelled events removed after 30 days</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="btn btn-outline btn-block" href="/login">Get started free</a>
        </div>
        <div class="card price-card featured">
          <span class="price-ribbon">Most popular</span>
          <div class="price-tier">Premium</div>
          <div class="price-amount"><b>$10</b><span>/ month *</span></div>
          <div class="price-alt">or $100 / year *</div>
          <ul class="price-list">
            <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Unlimited active events</li>
            <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Unlimited attendees per event **</li>
            <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Host public or private events</li>
            <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Remove attendees from any hosted event</li>
            <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Create a group to host events</li>
            <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Create recurring events</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="price-note">
            <p>* billed in your local currency at the exchange rate on the day of purchase</p>
            <p>** attendees limited to 100 by default</p>
          </div>
          <a class="btn btn-accent btn-block" href="/login" style="margin-top:20px;">Sign in to upgrade</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">Groups</span>
        <h2>Together we excel</h2>
        <p>Whether it's a loose circle of friends or a formal group with membership and coordinated activities &mdash; we want to help you run it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="groups-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="groups-steps">
            <div class="gs-row">
              <div class="gs-num">1</div>
              <div>
                <h3>Creating and maintaining a group</h3>
                <p>Any Premium member can create one group per membership, and add up to five additional members as group moderators. A group must always be owned by a Premium member; ownership can be transferred by contacting support.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="gs-row">
              <div class="gs-num">2</div>
              <div>
                <h3>Benefits of running events as a group</h3>
                <p>Here's what your group unlocks &mdash; included with any Premium membership.</p>
                <ul class="gs-benefits">
                  <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Moderators can create &amp; manage events in the group's name</li>
                  <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Group events are shown as hosted by the group</li>
                  <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Groups are public by default</li>
                  <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Can restrict membership to invite&#8209;only</li>
                  <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> Can hold private events visible only to members</li>
                  <li><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="5 12.5 9.5 17 19 6.5"/></svg> All the benefits of Premium</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="card group-preview">
          <div class="gp-cover"></div>
          <div class="gp-body">
            <img class="gp-avatar" src="/design/categories/culture.jpg" alt="">
            <h4>Madrid Hikers Club</h4>
            <div class="gp-meta"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8.5"/><ellipse cx="12" cy="12" rx="3.6" ry="8.5"/><line x1="3.7" y1="9.5" x2="20.3" y2="9.5"/><line x1="3.7" y1="14.5" x2="20.3" y2="14.5"/></svg> Public group &middot; <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="9" cy="8.5" r="3.2"/><path d="M2.8 20c0-3.4 2.8-5.7 6.2-5.7s6.2 2.3 6.2 5.7"/><circle cx="17.2" cy="9.2" r="2.4"/><path d="M21.2 20c0-2.6-1.9-4.6-4.4-5.3"/></svg> 184 members</div>
            <div class="gp-mods">
              <img src="/design/avatar-placeholder.png" alt="">
              <img src="/design/avatar-placeholder.png" alt="">
              <img src="/design/avatar-placeholder.png" alt="">
              <span>3 moderators</span>
            </div>
            <div class="gp-event"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3.5" y="5" width="17" height="16" rx="2.5"/><line x1="3.5" y1="9.5" x2="20.5" y2="9.5"/><line x1="8" y1="3" x2="8" y2="7"/><line x1="16" y1="3" x2="16" y2="7"/></svg> Hosting &ldquo;Sunset ridge walk&rdquo; &middot; Sat, 6:30 PM</div>
            <p class="gp-sample-tag">Sample group shown for illustration</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="foot-grid">
        <div>
          <h4>About us</h4>
          <!-- Real links as of M9 (they were inert placeholder spans
               until these pages existed). -->
          <a href="/feedback">Feedback</a>
          <a href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>
          <a href="/terms">Terms and conditions</a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4>Services</h4>
          <a href="/events">Events</a>
          <a href="/groups">Groups</a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4>ExpatEvents, a Bald Traveler site</h4>
          <p class="foot-tagline">Building an expat community by helping you socialize with other expats.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="foot-bottom">&copy; ExpatEvents. All rights reserved.</div>
    </div>
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
